cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "RMT Portfolio: Random Matrix Theory denoising of covariance matrices for portfolio construction"
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end empirical study of covariance-matrix estimation for portfolio
  construction. Sample covariance is compared against Ledoit-Wolf linear
  shrinkage, constant-correlation shrinkage, Marchenko-Pastur hard and soft
  thresholding, nonlinear shrinkage (RIE/QuEST), and a PCA factor model, across
  six allocators (equal weight, inverse variance, minimum variance, risk parity,
  hierarchical risk parity, maximum diversification) and three market panels
  (US sector ETFs, Chinese sector ETFs, and a high-aspect-ratio US single-stock
  universe). Rolling out-of-sample backtests include proportional transaction
  costs and turnover. The central finding is that ex-ante risk-forecast quality
  (Patton QLIKE loss) discriminates between estimators where realised Sharpe
  ratios do not: nonlinear shrinkage is the only estimator that improves
  forecast accuracy consistently, by 15-21% across the three panels, with the
  gain increasing in the aspect ratio q = N/T.
authors:
  - name: "RMT Portfolio contributors"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2025-12-31"
license: MIT
